# Claude Code - Git Ignore Recommendations

# If your claude.json contains sensitive data like API keys,
# you should add it to your .gitignore:

.claude/claude.json

# Alternative: Keep claude.json in git but use environment variables
# for sensitive data, then this file can be committed safely.

# You may want to ignore personal preferences or local customizations:
# .claude/local-overrides.json

# Keep these files in version control (recommended):
# .claude/README.md
# .claude/QUICK_REFERENCE.md
# .claude/instructions/
# .claude/workflows/

# Note: The current configuration has the Figma API key in claude.json.
# Consider moving to environment variable:
#
# Before:
#   "--figma-api-key=figd_..."
#
# After:
#   "--figma-api-key=${FIGMA_API_KEY}"
#
# Then set in your environment:
#   export FIGMA_API_KEY="figd_..."
